      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(aws): bootstrap SSH over Tailscale hostname when enabled",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWith `--network tailscale` on the AWS provider, bootstrap readiness probes\nand SSH targets always used the instance public IPv4. When the crabbox\noperator runs on EC2 in the same account/region, AWS drops EC2→EC2\npublic-IP traffic without VPC peering. The leased box joins the tailnet\nvia cloud-init and is reachable there, but `warmup` hangs on the public\nIP probe until timeout.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```console\n$ go test ./internal/providers/aws/ -count=1 -run TestBootstrapSSHHost\nok  github.com/openclaw/crabbox/internal/providers/aws\n\n# Host selection contract:\n# Tailscale enabled  → rendered/explicit hostname (not public IP)\n# Tailscale disabled → public IPv4 unchanged\n\n$ CI on PR: Go, Docs, Worker, Scripts, Apple VM, connectors — all green (12 checks)\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** AWS warmup probes public IP under Tailscale, unusable from EC2 operators\n- **Real environment tested:** unit tests + full crabbox CI on fix/aws-tailscale-bootstrap-probe\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:** `go test ./internal/providers/aws/ -run TestBootstrapSSHHost`; GitHub Actions matrix\n- **Evidence after fix:** unit proof of host selection; acquire + resolve paths use `sshTargetForBootstrap`; CI green\n- **Observed result after fix:** Tailscale-enabled configs select hostname; disabled keep public IP\n- **What was not tested:** live `crabbox warmup --network tailscale` from an EC2 operator (requires AWS + Tailscale auth)\n\n## Summary\n\n- When `Tailscale.Enabled`, use rendered/explicit Tailscale hostname for bootstrap SSH host\n- Apply on acquire and resolve (instance id + alias)\n- Unit coverage for host selection\n\nCloses #1049\n",
